{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that each parameter (`beta0`, `theta`, and `sigma`) receives its built-in prior before being used in the likelihood. This is a mechanical same-density change because Stan log-density contributions are additive. The protected observation `y` remains a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with `poisson_log`. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0> y; // count outcomes
  vector<lower=0>[N] E; // exposure
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] log_E = log(E);
}
parameters {
  real beta0; // intercept
  vector[N] theta; // heterogeneous random effects
  real<lower=0> sigma; // non-centered re variance 
}
model {
  beta0 ~ normal(0.0, 2.5);
  theta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 5);
  y ~ poisson_log(log_E + beta0 + theta * sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  vector[N] eta = log_E + beta0 + theta * sigma;
  vector[N] mu = exp(eta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"E":[2.9457970788847416,0.3385527035859187,3.1761085437355527],"N":3,"y":[2,2,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
